---
import {
  eazeArchitecture as architecture,
  eazeJourney as journey,
  eazeOwnership as ownership,
} from "@/data/eazegames-case-study";
---

<section id="architecture-and-ownership" class="wrap region stack" aria-labelledby="ownership-title">
  <p class="kick"><span class="idx">03</span> Architecture & ownership</p>
  <h2 id="ownership-title" class="section-title">
    Frontend responsibility, with integration boundaries made explicit.
  </h2>
  <p class="eaze-ownership-statement">
    I joined the initial two-person team, helped take the original frontend from an empty repository to production, and
    created the reusable component and utility foundation used as the frontend team expanded to six.
  </p>

  <div class="eaze-ownership-grid">
    <div class="panel stack">
      <h3 class="panel-title">My frontend scope</h3>
      <ul class="eaze-list">
        {ownership.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="panel stack">
      <h3 class="panel-title">Not claimed as my implementation</h3>
      <ul class="eaze-list">
        <li>Backend services and WebSocket servers</li>
        <li>Game-engine or game-provider implementation</li>
        <li>Pay.nl or payment-provider infrastructure</li>
        <li>Legal, compliance, fraud, or regulatory systems</li>
        <li>The current interface or later product versions</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figure class="eaze-architecture-figure">
    <div
      class="eaze-architecture-map"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Frontend architecture map showing the browser SPA connected to six owned frontend areas and clearly labeled external integration boundaries"
      aria-describedby="eaze-architecture-caption eaze-architecture-text"
    >
      <div class="eaze-architecture-root">
        <span>BROWSER SPA</span>
        <strong>React · Redux · JavaScript</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="eaze-architecture-routes" aria-hidden="true">
        {
          architecture.map((group) => (
            <div class="eaze-architecture-node" data-boundary={group.boundary ? "external" : "frontend"}>
              <span>{group.boundary ? "INTEGRATION BOUNDARY" : "FRONTEND SCOPE"}</span>
              <strong>{group.title}</strong>
              <small>{group.items.join(" · ")}</small>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption id="eaze-architecture-caption">
      A newly drawn frontend map. Backend services, WebSocket servers, Pay.nl, and game providers are shown only as
      integration boundaries.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p id="eaze-architecture-text" class="eaze-boundary-text">
    Text equivalent: the browser SPA owned shared UI, authentication and RBAC surfaces, competition/catalog state,
    WebSocket-driven presentation, payment and wallet UI, internationalization, and frontend delivery. Backend,
    payment-provider, game-provider, and WebSocket server implementations remained external boundaries.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="wrap region stack" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
  <p class="kick"><span class="idx">04</span> Original user journey</p>
  <h2 id="journey-title" class="section-title">One product shell across acquisition, play, and account state.</h2>
  <ol class="eaze-journey">
    {
      journey.map((step, index) => (
        <li>
          <>
            <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            <strong>{step}</strong>
          </>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
</section>
